    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0211" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg137"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1789.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-06-16"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            16, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I will thank you to bring to the attention
                    of her Majesty’s government he enclosed copy of a representation made by a
                    number of gentlemen of Hart, ford, Connecticut, in regard to the case of Thomas
                    J. Hynes, who, it appears as improperly imprisoned in Ireland by the British
                    officers. The necessity of his application may be removed by the release of Mr.
                    Hynes anterior to the ate of this despatch, but if this be not the case you may
                    request information concerning the reasons which warrant a continued
                    detention.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>






